Subject: [PATCH 46/49] fix(ui): the dock menu's faces are pictures, following
 is a row

The reviewer dock's menu trigger drew the presence stack (PeerAvatars),
whose faces are buttons of their own: a person's face follows them, an
agent's flies the camera to its frame. Inside the trigger, a click on a
face did both, so opening the menu started following whoever was there.

The trigger now draws plain faces (yours first, up to three, then a "+N"
disc) and nothing inside it is a button. What a face did moves into the
menu, one row per person or agent under "Here now": a person's row
follows them (and stops), an agent's goes to where it works, disabled
while doop cannot tell where that is. PeerAvatars exports presenceLabel
and flyToPresence for it; the full layout's stack is unchanged.

Test: reviewerLayoutBrowser has a peer in the room, finds no button
inside the trigger, opens the menu with nobody followed, and follows the
peer from their row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
